(2040, 'step-by-step-guide-to-creating-a-transportable-brf-initiator-rule-in-sap-grc-msmp', 'Jagan', 'Sunkara.jagan@gmail.com', 'Thank you very much for the detail article. this really helps a lot for the technical people', 'approved', '2026-03-17 07:56:22', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(2041, 'mastering-sap-grc-ruleset-manager-a-complete-overview', 'Prasad Annam', 'annam.annam6585@gmail.com', 'Thanks Raghu for your Insights on GRAC Ruleset Manager. Looking more to hear from you and Excited.\n\nThank you!', 'approved', '2026-03-18 01:27:43', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(2043, 'what-actually-optimizes-sap-licenses-star-usmm-lawslaw-explained', 'Srinivas', 'srinip262@gmail.com', 'Yes Chetan. Rightly mentioned. STAR analysis is only for S/4HANA systems. SAP is not focusing on ECC anymore and thus any tools/solutions that SAP is developing will be for S/4HANA. I also experienced their SAM4U solution which does automate the licensing evaluation.. but for S/4 Users, these are License savers.', 'approved', '2026-03-27 14:52:56', NULL, NULL, 2035, NULL),
(2045, 'step-by-step-guide-to-creating-a-transportable-brf-initiator-rule-in-sap-grc-msmp', 'Shashi Kandari', 'shashi.kandari@gmail.com', 'Dear Sir,\n\nPlease also explain DB Lookup logic and implementation steps', 'approved', '2026-05-10 07:10:45', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(2046, 'sap-cloud-identity-services-architecture-ias-ips-sso', 'Rajan Mishra', 'mishra.rajan05011994@gmail.com', 'Great informative article', 'approved', '2026-05-15 20:53:46', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(2047, 'sap-derived-roles-adjustment-suprn-regenerate-dependent', 'Varun Kumar', 'nainivarun82@gmail.com', 'Thanks a lot, This was helpful for me while doing the rollout project where we having multiple derived roles created via VBS Scripting', 'approved', '2026-05-15 20:59:58', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(2048, 'sap-fiori-security-checklist-s4hana-projects', 'Srinivas', 'srinip262@gmail.com', 'Great article that explains about SAP Fiori in S/4HANA projects.', 'approved', '2026-05-18 05:46:49', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(2049, 'sap-firefighter-emergency-access-management-enhancements', 'Raj Varadarajan', 'rangavar84@gmail.com', 'Excellent Post! The enhancement feature of email notification and Audit report mitigates the risk and provide more visibility. However, as an auditor, i believe that the governance culture should be embedded in the process so that the players know exactly what is their responsibility and accountability. Before obtaining EAM request, purpose and timelines should be clearly stated and approved. The controller should periodically review the FFID access and ensure that this is still valid.', 'approved', '2026-05-18 21:28:12', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(2050, 'sap-iag-vs-sap-grc-access-control', 'Raj Varadarajan', 'rangavar84@gmail.com', 'Very Insightful and clearly explained about GRC vs IAG', 'approved', '2026-05-18 21:49:45', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(2051, 'ai-transforming-sap-security', 'Srinivas', 'srinip262@gmail.com', 'Excellent insights on how AI is reshaping the future of SAP Security. The article rightly highlights that AI is no longer just an innovation layer - it is becoming a core enabler for intelligent access governance, anomaly detection, risk prediction, and continuous compliance in complex SAP landscapes.\n\nWhat stands out is the practical perspective on balancing automation with governance and human oversight. As SAP environments continue to expand across cloud, BTP, and hybrid ecosystems, AI-driven security capabilities will become essential rather than optional.\n\nA very relevant and timely read for SAP Security, GRC, and Cybersecurity professionals. Great contribution by the team at SAP Security Expert.', 'approved', '2026-05-23 01:42:35', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(2052, 'ai-transforming-sap-security', 'Inderdeep Singh', 'redninow@gmail.com', 'A very well-articulated; deep insights into how AI is transforming SAP Security from traditional rule-based governance to intelligent, behaviour-driven risk management. The way the article connects AI, SoD, governance maturity, and the future role of SAP Security professionals is very practical and forward-thinking. A very informative and industry-relevant for modern SAP security professionals.', 'approved', '2026-05-23 18:06:44', '2026-05-24 02:59:07', 'A very well-articulated &amp; deep insights into how AI is transforming SAP Security from traditional rule-based governance to intelligent, behaviour-driven risk management. The way the article connects AI, SoD, governance maturity, and the future role of SAP Security professionals is very practical and forward-thinking. A very informative and industry-relevant for modern SAP security professionals.', NULL, NULL),
(2053, 'step-by-step-guide-to-creating-a-transportable-brf-initiator-rule-in-sap-grc-msmp', 'Swathi Kankanala', 'swathiknknl@gmail.com', 'Wonderful Article Sir!', 'approved', '2026-05-26 19:14:37', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(2054, 'step-by-step-guide-to-creating-a-transportable-brf-initiator-rule-in-sap-grc-msmp', 'Swathi Kankanala', 'swathiknknl@gmail.com', 'Wonderful Article Sir!', 'approved', '2026-05-26 19:14:37', '2026-05-26 19:35:31', 'Wonderful Article Sir!', NULL, NULL),
(2055, 'sap-authorization-combinations-that-break-controls', 'Mari Tuunainen', 'Mari.e.tuunainen@gmail.com', 'I wonder how typical direct table access still is.\n\nOne would think that with all the fancy Analytics platforms, and embedded Fiori analytics, organizations would be more willing to let go of letting anyone access the raw data and build their own reports that may or may not be based on solid logic - but sadly even suggesting restricting direct table maintain access is met with strong change resistance', 'approved', '2026-05-31 17:26:40', '2026-05-31 18:05:51', 'I wonder how typical direct table access still is.\n\n One would think that with all the fancy Analytics platforms, and embedded Fiori analytics, organizations would be more willing to let go of letting &quot;anyone&quot; access the raw data and build their own reports that may or may not be based on solid logic - but sadly even suggesting restricting direct table maintain access is met with strong change resistance', NULL, NULL),
(2056, 'how-to-prepare-your-sap-landscape-for-indias-dpdpa', 'Srinivas', 'srinip262@gmail.com', 'Great article!! Clear, practical, and exceptionally well-articulated on the DPDP Act. It addresses the key implementation considerations that many organizations are currently juggling with. The timing couldn\'t be better, and the insights provided are both relevant and actionable. This is exactly the kind of guidance I was looking for as we advance our DPDP compliance journey.', 'approved', '2026-05-31 19:59:54', '2026-05-31 21:04:17', 'Great article!! Clear, practical, and exceptionally well-articulated on the DPDP Act. It addresses the key implementation considerations that many organizations are currently juggling with. The timing couldn&#039;t be better, and the insights provided are both relevant and actionable. This is exactly the kind of guidance I was looking for as we advance our DPDP compliance journey.', NULL, NULL),
(2057, 'how-to-prepare-your-sap-landscape-for-indias-dpdpa', 'Shravanth Arisetty', 'shravanth@threatsenseai.com', 'This is one of the most practical and well-structured guides I\'ve come across for aligning SAP landscapes with India\'s DPDPA. What sets it apart is how it bridges the gap between legal obligation and technical execution, something most compliance articles fail to do.\n\nThe mapping of Data Principal rights directly to SAP capabilities (ILM, IRT, RAL, EoP) is exactly the kind of operational clarity that CISOs, DPOs, and SAP architects need to move from awareness to action. The penalty breakdown, especially the point about a single incident triggering multiple penalty categories simultaneously, is a wake-up call that every CFO and Board should read.\n\nFor any Indian enterprise running SAP, this should be required reading before your next compliance review.', 'approved', '2026-05-31 21:01:58', '2026-05-31 21:03:55', 'This is one of the most practical and well-structured guides I&#039;ve come across for aligning SAP landscapes with India&#039;s DPDPA. What sets it apart is how it bridges the gap between legal obligation and technical execution, something most compliance articles fail to do.\n\nThe mapping of Data Principal rights directly to SAP capabilities (ILM, IRT, RAL, EoP) is exactly the kind of operational clarity that CISOs, DPOs, and SAP architects need to move from awareness to action. The penalty breakdown, especially the point about a single incident triggering multiple penalty categories simultaneously, is a wake-up call that every CFO and Board should read.\n\nFor any Indian enterprise running SAP, this should be required reading before your next compliance review.', NULL, NULL),
(2058, 'auditing-sap-s4hana-cloud-public-edition-practitioners-guide', 'Inderdeep Singh', 'redninow@gmail.com', 'Excellent article with a very practical approach towards auditing SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition. I particularly liked how the article explained the shared responsibility model and translated cloud-specific audit requirements into actionable audit checkpoints. The coverage of security, compliance, access governance, and audit readiness provides valuable guidance for both auditors and SAP security practitioners. This is the kind of content that helps bridge the gap between traditional SAP audit methodologies and modern cloud ERP environments. Looking forward to more deep-dive articles on SAP S/4 HANA Public Cloud security and governance topics.', 'approved', '2026-05-31 21:24:14', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
